@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### List movies (paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?page=1&limit=20

### Search movies by title
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?search=matrix

### Get a single movie by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### Get a movie that doesn't exist (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/999999

### --- Admin-only actions ---
### Run "Login as seeded admin user" in auth.http first so the auth cookie is set,
### then run the requests below in the same REST Client session.

### Create a movie (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Sample Movie",
  "description": "A movie created via the .http test client.",
  "genre": "Drama",
  "releaseDate": "2024-01-15",
  "posterUrl": "https://example.com/poster.jpg"
}

### Update a movie (admin only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Sample Movie (Updated)",
  "description": "Updated description.",
  "genre": "Drama",
  "releaseDate": "2024-01-15",
  "posterUrl": "https://example.com/poster.jpg"
}

### Delete a movie (admin only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### --- Error / authorization cases ---

### Create a movie while logged out or as non-admin (expect 401/403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should Fail",
  "description": "No permission.",
  "genre": "Drama",
  "releaseDate": "2024-01-15"
}

### Create a movie with invalid payload (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "genre": "",
  "releaseDate": "not-a-date"
}
